---
import '../styles/global.css';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>Field Relay — reconciliation case study</title>
    <style>
      .case-study {
        max-width: 820px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: clamp(32px, 8vw, 96px) 24px;
      }
      .case-study h1 {
        margin-bottom: 20px;
      }
      .case-study h2 {
        margin-top: 42px;
      }
      .case-study p {
        max-width: 670px;
        color: #46564e;
        line-height: 1.7;
      }
      .case-study .lede {
        font-size: 1.05rem;
      }
      .case-study a {
        font-weight: 700;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="case-study">
      <p class="eyebrow">FIELD RELAY / CASE STUDY</p>
      <h1>A review desk for the difference between two exports.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Field Relay is a browser-local reconciliation desk for comparing a baseline export with a
        candidate export before someone acts. It keeps exact input, original source rows, field
        mapping, and local review decisions in an explicit download.
      </p>
      <h2>Comparison design</h2>
      <p>
        Each export has its own explicit business-ID map and selected comparable fields. IDs remain
        literal strings, so leading zeroes are preserved. One-to-one records can be unchanged or
        changed; records only on one side stay visible. Duplicate or blank IDs stay ambiguous with
        all row evidence and never receive an automatic replacement decision.
      </p>
      <h2>Reviewable evidence</h2>
      <p>
        A reviewer can record an explicit hold, a proposal to use Candidate as current, or an
        expected difference, with a reason. These decisions bind to the exact local input and
        mapping revision. Editing either export, a map, a compared field, or whitespace
        normalization clears them. The report includes full input text once in a shared comparison
        reference, then maps review decisions to that reference with mappings, findings, and
        unresolved items. Diagnostic fingerprints are labels only.
      </p>
      <h2>Separate delivery lab</h2>
      <p>
        The earlier fictional delivery exercise remains separate from reconciliation. It
        demonstrates parsing, approval, outage retry, and a replay-safe ledger, but it does not
        consume comparison results or update any downstream system.
      </p>
      <h2>Operational boundary</h2>
      <p>
        The reconciliation desk reads pasted or browser-selected files only in the active tab and
        never sends them to a server. Exports are explicit downloads. The included examples and
        delivery lab are fictional; the comparison workflow works with a user’s own CSV exports.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href={base}>Open the reconciliation desk</a> · <a
          href="https://github.com/mastodonsharkgirl/field-relay">Inspect the source</a
        >
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
